  "AICL is the licensing and transaction layer built on top of AICR. Where AICR declares what is allowed, AICL defines how permission is actually obtained: license tiers and prices, quote and payment endpoints, signed license tokens, usage and audit logs, and revocation. It is designed to interoperate with emerging machine-payment mechanisms such as HTTP 402 flows and pay-per-crawl schemes, with agentic payment kept inside human-approved budgets and audit trails.": "A AICL a licensing me a transaction layer el lilecha el mo er a bab er a AICR. A AICR a olecha ngerang a sebechel, e a AICL a olsisechakl rolel a klisiich el kongei a meral: license tiers me a prices, quote me a payment endpoints, signed license tokens, usage me a audit logs, me a revocation. Ng lilecha el kirel a kaiuereor loba beches el machine-payment mechanisms el ua HTTP 402 me a pay-per-crawl, e a agentic payment a ngar chelsel a budget el mla lomdasu a chad me a audit trails.",
